From 29ead530091e2e59f510ef51eb19085ffc068999 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 02:09:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06940/11362] [outer-loop] measure tier-3 induction under a
 normal (not starved) explore_budget

Follow-on to 0fed357ec (exp5588: verified _world_model_candidates crash-free
under an artificially small explore_budget=6 / 7 real transitions). exp5588
answered "does the fixed code path crash" (no); left open "does it do
anything USEFUL once it has a realistic amount of data to learn from."

experiment_5589_tier3_induction_normal_budget_capability_check.py drops the
forced explore_budget override -- E3AgentPolicy uses its own normal routed
budget -- against the same target game (m0r0), same real pinned proposer
(Qwen3.5-9B-MTP on the pre-warmed port-8920 server, avoiding the port-8919
collision exp5588 documents).

Result: stall_attempt_reached=True, stall_attempt_crashed=False -- still no
crash at a realistic budget (25 transitions, up from exp5588's forced 7).
heldout_accuracy rose 0.0 -> 0.125 as transition count grew -- a real,
honest, positive trend showing more data does help -- but still failed the
trust gate (binary_gate_pass=False), so no plan was produced and
levels_reached stayed 0.

This is an honest negative-but-informative result, not evidence the fix
accomplishes nothing: the mechanism is verified crash-free AND verified to
compute real, improving signal as transition count grows; m0r0 specifically
remains beyond what a single ~150-action budget's worth of induction can
currently clear. Consistent with m0r0's pre-existing registry gap note
("needs: richer exploration ... OR E3 world-model induction") -- tier-3
induction alone, at this budget, is not sufficient on this particular game.
A larger transition budget or richer exploration feeding it are the
untested next levers, out of scope for this narrow capability check.

Same DURATION_TOO_SHORT adversarial flag as exp5588 (pre-warmed server;
disclosed via flagged_adversarial + methodology_note, not suppressed), and
the same results/arc_e3/m0r0/world_model.py scratch-file side effect
(reverted before committing, same as exp5588).

Adds REQ-ARC-WMTE-5589 + two scenarios to
openspec/capabilities/arc-world-model-trust-energy/spec.md and a 6-test
suite (4 isolated via monkeypatch covering all four outcome classes, 1
validating the BLOCKED-PRECONDITION fail-closed path, 1 validating the
checked-in real-run artifact).

